# SGIT Autonomous Student Dashboard Architecture + CGPA + Persistence + College Image Polish

This implementation plan outlines the architecture, database schema, API endpoints, and UI refinements required to update the SGIT student portal according to institutional specifications.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Top Navigation Removal**: The horizontal top navbar for logged-in students will be removed completely. The student portal will exclusively use a sticky left sidebar on desktop and a drawer sidebar on mobile.
> - **Database Persistence**: Academic records (semesters, subjects, marks, credits, grades, SGPA, CGPA) will be stored in MongoDB under the student's account. Saved data will persist across browser refreshes and logouts.
> - **SGIT Grading System**: SGIT standard grade bounds (S >= 90, A = 80-89, B = 70-79, C = 60-69, D = 50-59, E = 40-49, F < 40, Ab = Absent) and degree class thresholds will be enforced and made configurable in the Super Admin panel.

